    {
      "id": "tools:journeys",
      "file": "data/journeys.json",
      "path": "/start",
      "title": "Guided learning routes",
      "revision": "caeff4a1dc6f61e53929e6cd2fd8e5291b8937ab89db46868d4cd9fcd8f77503",
      "checked": "2026-10-05",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "tool-text-8f6e4b1ba5969cba",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.voters.title",
          "text": "Who has a vote?",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-11cf318345d4dcc3",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.voters.text",
          "text": "Knesset elections choose a national legislature. Citizenship, residency and location are different questions: people affected by Israeli decisions do not all have a vote in this election. Begin with the citizenship and residency distinctions.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-ec6b5eafee07b3ba",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.voters.link",
          "text": "Read who votes",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-f2884bcb4106c89f",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.voters.question",
          "text": "Does living under the effects of a government's decisions automatically give someone a Knesset vote?",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-d61f542e82e321c2",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.voters.options.0",
          "text": "Yes, every resident has the same national voting rights",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-e03c33090e5c54b6",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.voters.options.1",
          "text": "No; eligibility depends on citizenship and other legal conditions",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-382ffeb5342d044c",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.voters.explanation",
          "text": "National and municipal eligibility differ. The guide distinguishes citizens, East Jerusalem permanent residents and Palestinians in the occupied West Bank and Gaza.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-b32e9a66e7b06cb8",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.seats.title",
          "text": "Votes become 120 seats",
          "numbers": [
            "120"
          ],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-4dfdd9d90d0503a7",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.seats.text",
          "text": "Voters choose a ranked electoral list in one nationwide constituency. A list needs 3.25% of valid votes to receive seats. Votes for a list below the threshold are not transferred to another list; seats are allocated among the lists that pass.",
          "numbers": [
            "3.25%"
          ],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-d08702dc0293a072",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.seats.link",
          "text": "See how votes become seats",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-7d7987df5630d7c3",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.seats.question",
          "text": "What happens to votes cast for a list below the threshold?",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-d967c1538b1c8981",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.seats.options.0",
          "text": "They are transferred to its closest ally",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-c18c3b3aad297741",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.seats.options.1",
          "text": "They produce no seats for that list",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-60ef571f5d782515",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.seats.explanation",
          "text": "The threshold applies to valid votes. Passing lists share the seats; surplus-vote agreements operate between eligible passing lists, not as a rescue for a failed list.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-15cc5fa2b170e470",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.parties.title",
          "text": "A party is not a bloc",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-00baafb25f3ccf6b",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.parties.text",
          "text": "An electoral list can contain several parties. A bloc is a grouping used to describe possible alliances; it is not a single ballot choice. Read two profiles, then compare the same parties on one concrete question.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-b57fb891c0c222de",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.parties.link",
          "text": "Explore the parties",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-d9dd7ef874b57dcb",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.parties.question",
          "text": "If two lists belong to the same bloc, do they necessarily share every policy?",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-835d571f88b47a67",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.parties.options.0",
          "text": "Yes; a bloc is one party with one platform",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-cee0e361ea484e93",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.parties.options.1",
          "text": "No; cooperation can coexist with policy differences",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-b348f06a9937c455",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.parties.explanation",
          "text": "Blocs describe groupings, not complete agreement. Compare recorded positions and missing evidence before describing a shared agenda.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-db43a203fbbd937c",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.govern.title",
          "text": "Who can form a government?",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-ea8262f9d3a13345",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.govern.text",
          "text": "The largest list does not automatically govern. It needs a governing arrangement and Knesset confidence. An absolute seat majority is 61 of 120; that planning target does not by itself establish how a confidence vote will go or whether parties will cooperate.",
          "numbers": [
            "120",
            "61"
          ],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-0894b700aa0c2e7c",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.govern.link",
          "text": "Try a governing arrangement",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-20f471b1dcdf095b",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.govern.question",
          "text": "Does winning the largest number of seats guarantee that a list forms the government?",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-28fa389606a8ab1d",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.govern.options.0",
          "text": "Yes; the largest list automatically governs",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-7cab89e7880dd42a",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.govern.options.1",
          "text": "No; it still needs an arrangement that can win confidence",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-5a6bdad49febd1dd",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.govern.explanation",
          "text": "Seat arithmetic, recorded commitments and policy cooperation are separate questions. The formation guide explains the legal process; the builder helps you explore the arithmetic and constraints.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-0bf73e0a30587b34",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.compare.title",
          "text": "Compare one real question",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-b6b22deec5f3ce53",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.compare.text",
          "text": "Choose two or more lists in Compare. Find one shared recorded position and one difference. Open the evidence: what was said, when, and what remains unknown? A category count is not a forecast of governing stability.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-0723e9239d1f0034",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.compare.link",
          "text": "Compare recorded positions",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-693a98c884e4bf78",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.compare.question",
          "text": "What can missing evidence establish?",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-fe74ef417f41df07",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.compare.options.0",
          "text": "That parties agree because no disagreement is recorded",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-c9b3da220b8d2a18",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.compare.options.1",
          "text": "That the evidence is incomplete",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-016b0608e7587e90",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "steps.compare.explanation",
          "text": "Silence is not agreement. Look for complete dated evidence and distinguish a shared objective from agreement on how to achieve it.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": true
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-afd08855fa3f9bfe",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "routes.0.title",
          "text": "I have five minutes",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-756cc6b70314efda",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "routes.0.description",
          "text": "The essential distinctions, with one tool to try.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-1db0d2b16566429a",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "routes.0.nextLabel",
          "text": "Read the polls with these distinctions in mind",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-29a2d02a118d9dd3",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "routes.1.title",
          "text": "Help me understand the parties",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-ecc2a3a2322bf453",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "routes.1.description",
          "text": "From ballot choices to recorded disagreements and governing arrangements.",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        },
        {
          "id": "tool-text-71364f374cd2acfe",
          "kind": "text",
          "field": "routes.1.nextLabel",
          "text": "Read an issue in depth",
          "numbers": [],
          "links": [],
          "names": [],
          "negated": false
        }
      ],
      "links": [],
      "numbers": [
        "120",
        "120",
        "3.25%",
        "61"
      ]
    },
